{
 "version": 1,
 "title": "Power Down",
 "category": "Effects",
 "text": "Sound: a machine (or a tape) winding down: hold a note, and when you let go its pitch sags and falls away to nothing.\n\nHow it's built: one envelope with an instant attack, full sustain and a 1.5-second RELEASE. Its ENV opens the VCA; its INVERTED output (0 while the key is held, rising to 1 as it releases) is flipped by the Attenuverter into the oscillator's FM at 2 octaves: so when you let go, the pitch falls two octaves as the sound fades. Saw through a filter.\n\nPlay: hold a note, then let go.\n\nTweak: the envelope's RELEASE (how long it winds down), the oscillator's FM (how far it falls).",
 "voices": 1,
